From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: bootstrap: do not look for official plugins under the working directory

candidateBaseDirs() also returned process.cwd(), so each official plugin
was looked for at <cwd>/packages/<name>-plugin and as <name>-plugin in the
three directories above the working directory. A build that does not carry
the official plugins beside its entry point (anything but the SEA and
desktop builds) therefore loaded whatever a repository, or a shared
directory above it, put there: it was listed as a Z.ai plugin, enabled,
cached in ~/.zcode, and its MCP server command ran in every later session.
Official plugins and the bundled skills are only looked up beside the
entry point.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/bootstrap/src/app/bundled-plugins.ts	2026-09-25 10:16:23.127037645 +0200
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/packages/bootstrap/src/app/bundled-plugins.ts	2026-09-25 10:16:23.215047532 +0200
@@ -633,7 +633,7 @@
   // 修复原因：Electron app-server 运行在 resources/glm/zcode.cjs，官方插件资源也随桌面包
   // stage 到同级 packages/*-plugin。候选目录必须优先看入口文件目录，避免生产态退回到
   // monorepo-only 的 __dirname 查找假设。
-  return [entrypointDir(), runtimeDir(), process.cwd()].filter(
+  return [entrypointDir(), runtimeDir()].filter(
     (dir): dir is string => typeof dir === "string",
   );
 }
